==English==

===Etymology===
First attested in 1677.  From {{term|alkali|lang=en}}, ultimately from {{etyl|ar}} {{term|قلي|القلي|sc=Arab|tr=al-qaly|ashes of the [[saltwort]]}}, from {{term|قلى|sc=Arab|tr=qalā||to roast in a pan, fry}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈæl.kəl.aɪn/}}, {{SAMPA|/"{l.k@l.aIn/}}
* {{a|US}} {{enPR|ălˈkəlīn}}, {{IPA|/ˈæl.kə.laɪn/}}, {{SAMPA|/"{l.k@.laIn/}}
* {{audio|en-us-alkaline.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# An [[alkaline battery]].

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Of, or relating to an [[alkali]], one of a class of caustic bases.
# {{chemistry}} Having a [[pH]] greater than 7.

